<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="scenario_1_headings_applied_correctly" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 1 — Headings applied correctly</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a document with the following heading structure: Heading 1 "Installation" containing Heading 2 "Prerequisites"</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Heading</keyword>
        <keyword>Installation</keyword>
        <keyword>topic</keyword>
        <keyword>Headings</keyword>
        <keyword>applied</keyword>
        <keyword>correctly</keyword>
        <indexterm>Heading</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Installation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>topic</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
    <p>Consider a document with the following heading structure: Heading 1 "Installation" containing Heading 2 "Prerequisites" (concept) and Heading 2 "Install on Linux" (task).</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Headings applied correctly</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>.docx Style / Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>[Heading 1]: Installation [Heading 2]: Prerequisites [Heading 2]: Install on Linux</entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_byk_4wz_kkc">
&lt;map id="installation">
  &lt;title>Installation&lt;/title>
  &lt;topicref href="prerequisites.dita"/>
  &lt;topicref href="install_on_linux.dita"/>
&lt;/map></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>
            <b>Result:</b>The <b>Heading 1</b> section (<b>Installation</b>) creates a dedicated sub-map. Each <b>Heading 2</b> section becomes an individual DITA topic nested within that sub-map. The converter classifies topic types according to the content pattern following each heading:</p><ul id="ul_07233403">
            <li>
               <b>Prerequisites</b> → Concept topic</li>
            <li>
               <b>Install on Linux</b> → Task topic</li>
         </ul><p>This structure preserves both the document hierarchy and the semantic meaning of the content.</p>
  </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
